   "text": "I read the molecule as a macrocyclic peptide built from three residues, closed through a pyridine\u2013S\u2013benzene (diaryl sulfide) linker.\n\n**Peptide part**\n- The first residue is Dab (2,4-diaminobutyric acid). Its alpha carbon carries a CH2CH2NH2 side chain and is drawn with a wedge. Its alpha-NH is joined to a CH2 on the pyridine ring.\n- The second residue is Lys. Its alpha carbon is wedged to the (CH2)4NH2 chain. Its alpha-NH is joined to the Dab carbonyl.\n- The third residue is N-methyl-Trp. Its nitrogen carries a methyl group and is joined to the Lys carbonyl. The alpha carbon is wedged to CH2 and then to the indol-3-yl group. Its carbonyl is joined to an NH, which leads to a benzylic CH2.\n\n**Aromatic linker**\n- The pyridine has N1 and C2 bonded to S. C3 bears the CH2NH that connects to the Dab nitrogen.\n- The benzene ring has six substituted positions in order. C1 is bonded to S. C2 bears the CH2NH that connects to the Trp carbonyl. C3 bears a 4-carboxyphenyl group. C4 and C5 are CH. C6 bears Cl and sits next to C1.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nWorking out CIP priorities at each wedged centre gives S for Dab, Lys and Trp, matching the natural L-amino acids. I set @@ for the Dab carbon and @ for the Lys and Trp carbons to encode this.\n\nSMILES: NCC[C@@H]1NCc2cccnc2Sc2c(Cl)ccc(-c3ccc(C(=O)O)cc3)c2CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC1=O"
